Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-03-2000||04:46 PM||||Just thought I'd let you guys know that I finally got around to advancing my timing today and there's a definite difference in throttle reponse and it doesn't seem to ping at WOT under load.  It runs slightly warmer, but revvs quicker and has noticeably more "snap" off the line.  I advanced it about 4 degrees.  After it gets off the line, I don't think I can really tell a difference, but it's something.  I'm running 92 octane gas(sometimes 93.)  ||||reg||14
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||03-03-2000||09:05 PM||||Haaa!!! I knew it would work! That is good to hear. I mentioned this in another post and got mixed reviews. But I hear it is the way to go regarding better performance all the way around. I think I will do this next week. Can you give me more specifics on how you set the timing on your car? Thanks. ||||reg||1
